   "**A joint statement that names the arms supplier converts a local war into a test of Iran's word** — the direct effect of seven industrial democracies declaring in one voice that Iran must \"end its arming of and support\" for the Houthis, on the same day Iran's president arrives in New York to speak, is that the conflict is redefined from a Yemeni civil war into a compliance test with a named state; the compound consequence is that any future Houthi attack on shipping or on Saudi infrastructure will be read as Iran's answer, whether or not Tehran ordered it — which hands the Houthis the power to set Iran's diplomatic position for it, and hands Iran's adversaries a permanent justification for escalation",
