  "verse": "To your human sense and your human view are also connected your earthly jurisdictions, but you must not expect that these are equivalent with the strength of the character and of all virtues of the Creation Universal Consciousness nor with the Creation-given laws and recommendations to which your earthly courts and their laws do not even get close… between your understanding of the fairness and of the creational fairness… there is generally in the true sense of the word a scandalous and shaking difference.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 28, Verse 372",
  "hinge": "The cause here is not the bombing. It is the choice a state makes about how far its reckoning runs — whether it stops at the men who carried out the attack or continues to the officials whose lapse made it possible. The verse does not say earthly courts are evil; it says they fall short, and it names the direction of the shortfall: fairness that is narrow where creational fairness is total. Sri Lanka can serve the verdict it has and leave the second question to time, or it can answer it while the men who can answer it are still alive and still within its jurisdiction. Set the sentence honestly, publish the intelligence lapse, pay the compensation already ordered, and 2019 can begin to close. Leave the former intelligence chief's investigation to follow the former president's litigation, and what was convicted today will be the part of the story that was easiest to prove. Both are decisions, and the survivors at the demonstration line have already chosen which one they are waiting for."
